---
source: tests/compliance_snapshots.rs
---
{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "sbom-tools",
          "version": "[VERSION]",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/sbom-tool/sbom-tools",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SBOM-FRESHNESS",
              "name": "CraSbomFreshness",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(7) / Annex I Part II (1): SBOM freshness — timely regeneration after changes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(7) / Annex I Part II (1): SBOM freshness — timely regeneration after changes. References: CRA Art. 13(7); CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Regenerate the SBOM when components are added, removed, or updated. CRA Art. 13(7) requires manufacturers to systematically document relevant cybersecurity aspects, and the Annex I Part II (1) SBOM must reflect the product's current components. A creation timestamp later than the evaluation date is reported like a missing one: correct the generator's clock or time zone.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Regenerate the SBOM when components are added, removed, or updated. CRA Art. 13(7) requires manufacturers to systematically document relevant cybersecurity aspects, and the Annex I Part II (1) SBOM must reflect the product's current components. A creation timestamp later than the evaluation date is reported like a missing one: correct the generator's clock or time zone.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-MACHINE-READABLE",
              "name": "CraMachineReadableFormat",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM must be in a commonly used, machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.3+, or SPDX 3.0+)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM must be in a commonly used, machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.3+, or SPDX 3.0+). References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Ensure the SBOM is produced in CycloneDX 1.4+ (JSON or XML), SPDX 2.3+ (JSON or tag-value), or SPDX 3.0+ (JSON-LD). Older format versions may not be recognized as machine-readable under CRA Annex I Part II (1).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04",
                "markdown": "Ensure the SBOM is produced in CycloneDX 1.4+ (JSON or XML), SPDX 2.3+ (JSON or tag-value), or SPDX 3.0+ (JSON-LD). Older format versions may not be recognized as machine-readable under CRA Annex I Part II (1).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-17-CONTACT",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityContact",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(17): Single point of contact for vulnerability reporting (Annex I Part II (6), Annex II (2))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(17): Single point of contact for vulnerability reporting (Annex I Part II (6), Annex II (2)). References: CRA Art. 13(17); CRA Annex I Part II (6); CRA Annex II (2)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the product a single point of contact for vulnerability reports (Art. 13(17)): a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL referenced from the product component. securityContact or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar lowers the finding to Info.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(17) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex I Part II (6) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (2) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give the product a single point of contact for vulnerability reports (Art. 13(17)): a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL referenced from the product component. securityContact or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar lowers the finding to Info.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(17)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (6)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (2)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityMetadata",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability entries carry a severity or CVSS score"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability entries carry a severity or CVSS score. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every vulnerability entry a severity or CVSS score (Annex I Part II (4)). An entry whose VEX statement is not_affected and names a justification needs neither: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set vulnerabilities[].ratings[] on each entry with a severity (critical, high, medium, low) or a CVSS score.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a security_CvssV3VulnAssessmentRelationship (security_score, security_vectorString) for each vulnerability.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every vulnerability entry a severity or CVSS score (Annex I Part II (4)). An entry whose VEX statement is not\\_affected and names a justification needs neither: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set vulnerabilities\\[\\].ratings\\[\\] on each entry with a severity (critical, high, medium, low) or a CVSS score.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a security\\_CvssV3VulnAssessmentRelationship (security\\_score, security\\_vectorString) for each vulnerability.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA-REMEDIATION",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityRemediationDetail",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability remediations name a fixed version or describe the fix"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability remediations name a fixed version or describe the fix. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every vulnerability remediation a fixed version or a description of the fix (Annex I Part II (4)). A vulnerability whose VEX statement is not_affected and names a justification is exempt: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: an entry whose analysis.response declares update or workaround_available needs the details: set vulnerabilities[].recommendation to the fix (a fixed version or the steps to take), or vulnerabilities[].workaround to the workaround.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: the parser builds no remediation from this format, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 3.0 input.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every vulnerability remediation a fixed version or a description of the fix (Annex I Part II (4)). A vulnerability whose VEX statement is not\\_affected and names a justification is exempt: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** an entry whose analysis.response declares update or workaround\\_available needs the details: set vulnerabilities\\[\\].recommendation to the fix (a fixed version or the steps to take), or vulnerabilities\\[\\].workaround to the workaround.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** the parser builds no remediation from this format, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 3.0 input.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA-PROFILE",
              "name": "CraSecurityProfileConformance",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): SPDX 3.0 Security profile declared for a document that carries vulnerabilities"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): SPDX 3.0 Security profile declared for a document that carries vulnerabilities. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare SPDX 3.0 Security profile conformance when the document carries vulnerabilities, so the vulnerability information it conveys is complete (Annex I Part II (4)).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- SPDX 2.x: the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: list security in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare SPDX 3.0 Security profile conformance when the document carries vulnerabilities, so the vulnerability information it conveys is complete (Annex I Part II (4)).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** list security in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-5",
              "name": "CraLicensedComponentTracking",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): Third-party due diligence — license information for all components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): Third-party due diligence — license information for all components. References: CRA Art. 13(5)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record license information for every component to support the Art. 13(5) due diligence on integrated third-party components.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].licenses[] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages[].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing_LicenseExpression element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Record license information for every component to support the Art. 13(5) due diligence on integrated third-party components.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].licenses\\[\\] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages\\[\\].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing\\_LicenseExpression element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-5-PROFILE",
              "name": "CraLicensingProfileConformance",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile declared for a document that carries license data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile declared for a document that carries license data. References: CRA Art. 13(5)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile conformance when the document carries license data, so its Art. 13(5) licence evidence is conveyed completely.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- SPDX 2.x: the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: list simpleLicensing in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile conformance when the document carries license data, so its Art. 13(5) licence evidence is conveyed completely.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** list simpleLicensing in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-CVD-POLICY",
              "name": "CraCoordinatedDisclosure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (5): Coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy reference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (5): Coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy reference. References: CRA Annex I Part II (5); CRA Art. 13(8); prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy (Annex I Part II (5)) from the product component. In the CRA sidecar, coordinatedDisclosurePolicyUrl satisfies the open-source steward profile and vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl lowers the manufacturer finding to Info.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type advisories linking the policy.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) linking the policy to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory linking the policy to the root package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE",
                "markdown": "Reference the coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy (Annex I Part II (5)) from the product component. In the CRA sidecar, coordinatedDisclosurePolicyUrl satisfies the open-source steward profile and vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl lowers the manufacturer finding to Info.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type advisories linking the policy.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) linking the policy to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory linking the policy to the root package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-8",
              "name": "CraSupportPeriod",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / 13(19): Support period and security update end date (Annex II (7))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / 13(19): Support period and security update end date (Annex II (7)). References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Art. 13(19); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare when security updates end (Art. 13(8) / 13(19)): set supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar, or record the date in the SBOM.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.properties[] entry named end-of-support whose value is the date (RFC 3339 or YYYY-MM-DD).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- SPDX 3.0: validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 13(19) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare when security updates end (Art. 13(8) / 13(19)): set supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar, or record the date in the SBOM.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.properties\\[\\] entry named end-of-support whose value is the date (RFC 3339 or YYYY-MM-DD).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 13(19)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-8-EOL",
              "name": "CraEndOfLifeComponents",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8): Components past end-of-life, which receive no more security updates"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8): Components past end-of-life, which receive no more security updates. References: CRA Art. 13(8)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Upgrade or replace the components the end-of-life data marks as no longer supported: they receive no more security updates (Art. 13(8)).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Upgrade or replace the components the end-of-life data marks as no longer supported: they receive no more security updates (Art. 13(8)).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-LIFECYCLE",
              "name": "CraComponentLifecycle",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Component lifecycle and end-of-support status"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Component lifecycle and end-of-support status. References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record component lifecycle or end-of-support status (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)); supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar counts too.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add an eol, lifecycle or end-of-support entry to components[].properties[] (or an end-of-support date to metadata.component.properties[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- SPDX 3.0: validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Record component lifecycle or end-of-support status (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)); supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar counts too.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add an eol, lifecycle or end-of-support entry to components\\[\\].properties\\[\\] (or an end-of-support date to metadata.component.properties\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-LIFECYCLE-APPROACHING-EOL",
              "name": "CraApproachingEndOfLife",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Components reaching end-of-life within six months"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Components reaching end-of-life within six months. References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Plan replacements for the components the end-of-life data shows reaching end-of-life within six months (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Plan replacements for the components the end-of-life data shows reaching end-of-life within six months (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-15-PRODUCT",
              "name": "CraProductIdentification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(15): Product identification (Annex II (3))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(15): Product identification (Annex II (3)). References: CRA Art. 13(15); CRA Annex II (3)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the product the SBOM describes (Art. 13(15)); productName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info, but the SBOM should carry the name itself.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component.name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set the document name (DocumentName).\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(15) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (3) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Name the product the SBOM describes (Art. 13(15)); productName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info, but the SBOM should carry the name itself.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component.name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set the document name (DocumentName).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(15)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (3)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-VERSION",
              "name": "CraComponentVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component version identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component version identification. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Every component must have a version string. Use the actual release version (e.g., '1.2.3'), not a range or placeholder.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06",
                "markdown": "Every component must have a version string. Use the actual release version (e.g., '1.2.3'), not a range or placeholder.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-16",
              "name": "CraManufacturerIdentification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Manufacturer identification and contact information (Annex II (1))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Manufacturer identification and contact information (Annex II (1)). References: CRA Art. 13(16); CRA Annex II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the manufacturer as an organization creator of the SBOM (Art. 13(16)); manufacturerName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.manufacturer (name, contact[].email).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a creationInfo.creators[] entry \"Organization: Example Ltd (contact@example.com)\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to an Organization element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(16) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the manufacturer as an organization creator of the SBOM (Art. 13(16)); manufacturerName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.manufacturer (name, contact\\[\\].email).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry \"Organization: Example Ltd (contact@example.com)\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to an Organization element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(16)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-16-EMAIL",
              "name": "CraManufacturerEmail",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Valid manufacturer contact email (Annex II (1))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Valid manufacturer contact email (Annex II (1)). References: CRA Art. 13(16); CRA Annex II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide a valid contact email for the manufacturer. The email must contain an @ sign with valid local and domain parts.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: correct the metadata.manufacturer.contact[].email address.\n- SPDX 2.x: correct the address in the \"Organization: Name (email)\" creationInfo.creators[] entry.\n- SPDX 3.0: agent emails are not read from SPDX 3.0 documents, so this check does not apply.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(16) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide a valid contact email for the manufacturer. The email must contain an @ sign with valid local and domain parts.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** correct the metadata.manufacturer.contact\\[\\].email address.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** correct the address in the \"Organization: Name (email)\" creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** agent emails are not read from SPDX 3.0 documents, so this check does not apply.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(16)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-SUPPLIER",
              "name": "CraComponentSupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component supplier identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component supplier identification. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify each component's supplier; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03",
                "markdown": "Identify each component's supplier; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-STATEMENT",
              "name": "CraKnownVulnerabilities",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Documented vulnerability information — vulnerability data or assertion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Documented vulnerability information — vulnerability data or assertion. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Include the product's known vulnerabilities in the SBOM, or reference the vulnerability disclosure report (VDR) or VEX that states them (Annex I Part II (1)).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: list them in vulnerabilities[] with affects[].ref pointing at the affected components, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalReferences[] entry of type vulnerability-assertion or exploitability-statement.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field carries vulnerability data, and no external reference category names a VDR or VEX.\n- SPDX 3.0: add security_Vulnerability elements linked to the affected packages by affects Relationships, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType vulnerabilityDisclosureReport or vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Include the product's known vulnerabilities in the SBOM, or reference the vulnerability disclosure report (VDR) or VEX that states them (Annex I Part II (1)).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** list them in vulnerabilities\\[\\] with affects\\[\\].ref pointing at the affected components, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type vulnerability-assertion or exploitability-statement.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field carries vulnerability data, and no external reference category names a VDR or VEX.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add security\\_Vulnerability elements linked to the affected packages by affects Relationships, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType vulnerabilityDisclosureReport or vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-IDENTIFIER",
              "name": "CraComponentIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Unique identifier (PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID) on every component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Unique identifier (PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID) on every component. References: CRA Annex I; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID to each component for unique identification. PURLs are preferred (e.g., pkg:npm/lodash@4.17.21).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07",
                "markdown": "Add a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID to each component for unique identification. PURLs are preferred (e.g., pkg:npm/lodash@4.17.21).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-TRACEABILITY",
              "name": "CraPrimaryTraceability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Primary product component traceable across updates by a PURL or CPE"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Primary product component traceable across updates by a PURL or CPE. References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the primary product component a PURL or CPE so it can be traced across updates (Annex I Part II (1)); a SWHID or SWID alone does not satisfy this check.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component.purl (or cpe).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a PACKAGE-MANAGER purl or SECURITY cpe23Type packages[].externalRefs[] entry to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl on the rootElement package, or add a cpe23 externalIdentifier[] entry to it.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07",
                "markdown": "Give the primary product component a PURL or CPE so it can be traced across updates (Annex I Part II (1)); a SWHID or SWID alone does not satisfy this check.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component.purl (or cpe).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a PACKAGE-MANAGER purl or SECURITY cpe23Type packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl on the rootElement package, or add a cpe23 externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry to it.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-SUPPLY-CHAIN",
              "name": "CraDirectDependencySupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Supplier of every direct dependency identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, mandatory)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Supplier of every direct dependency identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, mandatory). References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the supplier of every direct dependency, one hop from the primary component or, when none is declared, from a root of the dependency graph (mandatory under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03",
                "markdown": "Identify the supplier of every direct dependency, one hop from the primary component or, when none is declared, from a root of the dependency graph (mandatory under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-SUPPLY-CHAIN-TRANSITIVE",
              "name": "CraTransitiveDependencySupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Suppliers of transitive dependencies identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, recommended)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Suppliers of transitive dependencies identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, recommended). References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the suppliers of transitive dependencies as well (recommended under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03",
                "markdown": "Identify the suppliers of transitive dependencies as well (recommended under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "CraComponentHash",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Component hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) for integrity verification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Component hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) for integrity verification. References: CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].hashes[] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- SPDX 2.x: add packages[].checksums[] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- SPDX 3.0: add verifiedUsing[] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-DEPENDENCY",
              "name": "CraDependencyRelationships",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Dependency relationships connect the primary component to its dependencies"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Dependency relationships connect the primary component to its dependencies. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add dependency relationships between components: connect the primary component to its direct dependencies and keep most components inside the dependency graph.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add dependencies[] entries (ref plus dependsOn[]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- SPDX 2.x: add relationships[] entries such as DEPENDS_ON (or DEPENDENCY_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- SPDX 3.0: add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Add dependency relationships between components: connect the primary component to its direct dependencies and keep most components inside the dependency graph.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add dependencies\\[\\] entries (ref plus dependsOn\\[\\]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add relationships\\[\\] entries such as DEPENDS\\_ON (or DEPENDENCY\\_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-DEPENDENCY-ROOTS",
              "name": "CraAmbiguousDependencyRoots",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Primary component identified when the dependency graph has several roots"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Primary component identified when the dependency graph has several roots. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the primary product component when the dependency graph has several roots, so the product's top-level dependencies are unambiguous.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- SPDX 2.x: name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- SPDX 3.0: set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the primary product component when the dependency graph has several roots, so the product's top-level dependencies are unambiguous.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-PRIMARY",
              "name": "CraPrimaryComponent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Top-level product component identified"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Top-level product component identified. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the top-level product component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- SPDX 2.x: name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- SPDX 3.0: set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the top-level product component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-CONTROLS",
              "name": "CraAnnexIControlEvidence",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I: Evidence URL for every control the CRA sidecar marks satisfied"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I: Evidence URL for every control the CRA sidecar marks satisfied. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every control the CRA sidecar's annexIPartIControls block marks satisfied an evidenceUrl pointing at its evidence (test report, design review, scan output), or set satisfied to false until the evidence exists.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every control the CRA sidecar's annexIPartIControls block marks satisfied an evidenceUrl pointing at its evidence (test report, design review, scan output), or set satisfied to false until the evidence exists.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-INVENTORY",
              "name": "CraInventory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM inventories the product's software components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM inventories the product's software components. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component and list the components in components[].\n- SPDX 2.x: list the packages in packages[] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- SPDX 3.0: add software_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component and list the components in components\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list the packages in packages\\[\\] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add software\\_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-DOC-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "CraDocumentIntegrity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Document integrity — serial number, hash, or digital signature"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Document integrity — serial number, hash, or digital signature. References: CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add document-level integrity metadata (Annex I Part I (2)(f)): a unique document serial number or namespace.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- SPDX 2.x: set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- SPDX 3.0: give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Add document-level integrity metadata (Annex I Part I (2)(f)): a unique document serial number or namespace.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-V",
              "name": "CraDeclarationOfConformity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex V: EU Declaration of Conformity reference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex V: EU Declaration of Conformity reference. References: CRA Annex V."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the EU Declaration of Conformity (Annex V): set ceMarkingReference in the CRA sidecar to the DoC's URL or document ID.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type attestation or certification-report pointing at the DoC also counts.\n- SPDX 2.x: a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory OTHER and referenceType declaration-of-conformity also counts.\n- SPDX 3.0: no reference type names a Declaration of Conformity, but an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation pointing at the DoC also counts.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex V (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the EU Declaration of Conformity (Annex V): set ceMarkingReference in the CRA sidecar to the DoC's URL or document ID.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type attestation or certification-report pointing at the DoC also counts.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory OTHER and referenceType declaration-of-conformity also counts.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** no reference type names a Declaration of Conformity, but an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation pointing at the DoC also counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex V](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-2",
              "name": "CraRiskAssessment",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(2): Reference to the documented cybersecurity risk assessment"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(2): Reference to the documented cybersecurity risk assessment. References: CRA Art. 13(2)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the documented cybersecurity risk assessment Art. 13(2) requires: set riskAssessmentUrl in the CRA sidecar to its URL or document reference.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type risk-assessment pointing at it also counts.\n- SPDX 2.x: no external reference category names a risk assessment, so use the sidecar key.\n- SPDX 3.0: an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType riskAssessment pointing at it also counts.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(2) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the documented cybersecurity risk assessment Art. 13(2) requires: set riskAssessmentUrl in the CRA sidecar to its URL or document reference.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type risk-assessment pointing at it also counts.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no external reference category names a risk assessment, so use the sidecar key.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType riskAssessment pointing at it also counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(2)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-PSIRT",
              "name": "CraPsirtUrl",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14: Public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14: Public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports. References: CRA Art. 14."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports (Art. 14 reporting readiness): set psirtUrl in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports (Art. 14 reporting readiness): set psirtUrl in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-EARLY-WARNING",
              "name": "CraEarlyWarningChannel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a): Channel for the 24-hour early warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a): Channel for the 24-hour early warning. References: CRA Art. 14(2)(a); CRA Art. 14(4)(a)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the channel for the 24-hour early warning of an actively exploited vulnerability or a severe incident (Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a)): set earlyWarningContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(2)(a) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 14(4)(a) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the channel for the 24-hour early warning of an actively exploited vulnerability or a severe incident (Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a)): set earlyWarningContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(2)(a)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 14(4)(a)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-NOTIFICATION",
              "name": "CraNotificationChannel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b): Channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b): Channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications. References: CRA Art. 14(2)(b); CRA Art. 14(4)(b)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications (Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b)): set incidentReportContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(2)(b) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 14(4)(b) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications (Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b)): set incidentReportContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(2)(b)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 14(4)(b)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-ENISA",
              "name": "CraEnisaPlatformIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(7): How the manufacturer reaches the ENISA single reporting platform"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(7): How the manufacturer reaches the ENISA single reporting platform. References: CRA Art. 14(7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the CSIRT designated as coordinator in enisaReportingPlatformId in the CRA sidecar: the one Art. 14(7) assigns by the manufacturer's main establishment and every notification selects on the ENISA Single Reporting Platform (https://portal.cra-srp.enisa.europa.eu/), through which Art. 14(1), (3) and (7) route notifications since 2026-09-11. Naming that CSIRT satisfies this finding. Do not register on the platform early to clear it: no registration is needed before a notification is due, and ENISA advises registering only then. A registration already made may be recorded instead. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Name the CSIRT designated as coordinator in enisaReportingPlatformId in the CRA sidecar: the one Art. 14(7) assigns by the manufacturer's main establishment and every notification selects on the ENISA Single Reporting Platform (https://portal.cra-srp.enisa.europa.eu/), through which Art. 14(1), (3) and (7) route notifications since 2026-09-11. Naming that CSIRT satisfies this finding. Do not register on the platform early to clear it: no registration is needed before a notification is due, and ENISA advises registering only then. A registration already made may be recorded instead. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-24",
              "name": "CraStewardVulnerabilityHandling",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 24: Open-source steward vulnerability-handling process (security contact or disclosure URL)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 24: Open-source steward vulnerability-handling process (security contact or disclosure URL)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Show the open-source steward's vulnerability-handling process (Art. 24): reference a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL from the product component, or set psirtUrl or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.",
                "markdown": "Show the open-source steward's vulnerability-handling process (Art. 24): reference a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL from the product component, or set psirtUrl or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-IV",
              "name": "CraEuccCertification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex IV: EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex IV: EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires. References: CRA Annex IV."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires: set euccProtectionProfileId, euccTargetOfEvaluation, euccItsefIdentifier or an unexpired euccValidUntil in the CRA sidecar. Once euccValidUntil has passed, the certificate is expired and none of these keys counts. The product classes are CRA Annex III (important, class I and II) and Annex IV (critical); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes which products each category covers.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: an externalReferences[] entry of type certification-report or attestation whose URL contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted, as is a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field is recognized as an EUCC reference, so use the sidecar keys.\n- SPDX 3.0: an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation whose locator contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex IV (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires: set euccProtectionProfileId, euccTargetOfEvaluation, euccItsefIdentifier or an unexpired euccValidUntil in the CRA sidecar. Once euccValidUntil has passed, the certificate is expired and none of these keys counts. The product classes are CRA Annex III (important, class I and II) and Annex IV (critical); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes which products each category covers.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** an externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type certification-report or attestation whose URL contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted, as is a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field is recognized as an EUCC reference, so use the sidecar keys.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation whose locator contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex IV](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-CREATOR",
              "name": "CraSbomCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM creator identified (person, organization or tool)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM creator identified (person, organization or tool)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify who created the SBOM: a person, organization or tool.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- SPDX 2.x: add creationInfo.creators[] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.",
                "markdown": "Identify who created the SBOM: a person, organization or tool.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SERIAL",
              "name": "CraDocumentIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM carries a unique document identifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM carries a unique document identifier."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the SBOM a unique document identifier.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- SPDX 2.x: set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- SPDX 3.0: give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId.",
                "markdown": "Give the SBOM a unique document identifier.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-NAME",
              "name": "CraComponentName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component has a name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component has a name."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every component a name; empty names and placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].name (PackageName), or files[].fileName for files.\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the element.",
                "markdown": "Give every component a name; empty names and placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].name (PackageName), or files\\[\\].fileName for files.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the element."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SPEC-VERSION",
              "name": "CraSpecVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Spec version sbom-tools reads (CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Spec version sbom-tools reads (CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use a spec version sbom-tools reads: CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0. An older version lacks fields the checks read, and what a newer version adds is not evaluated.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- SPDX 2.x: set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.",
                "markdown": "Use a spec version sbom-tools reads: CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0. An older version lacks fields the checks read, and what a newer version adds is not evaluated.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SPEC-VERSION-UNKNOWN",
              "name": "CraSpecVersionUnknown",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SPDX document declares a valid SPDX version"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SPDX document declares a valid SPDX version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare a valid SPDX version, 2.x or 3.0, so the document is read as the version it is.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- SPDX 2.x: set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.",
                "markdown": "Declare a valid SPDX version, 2.x or 3.0, so the document is read as the version it is.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ELEMENT-ID",
              "name": "CraElementIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every element has its own well-formed identifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every element has its own well-formed identifier."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every element its own well-formed identifier, the one dependency relationships refer to.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set a bom-ref on every component, one that differs from the component's name.\n- SPDX 2.x: give every element an SPDXID that starts with SPDXRef-.\n- SPDX 3.0: give every element an IRI spdxId.",
                "markdown": "Give every element its own well-formed identifier, the one dependency relationships refer to.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set a bom-ref on every component, one that differs from the component's name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** give every element an SPDXID that starts with SPDXRef-.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** give every element an IRI spdxId."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-PRODUCER",
              "name": "CraHardwareProducer",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Producer of every hardware component (device, firmware, driver)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Producer of every hardware component (device, firmware, driver). References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the producer (supplier or author) of every hardware component: device, firmware or device driver.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Name the producer (supplier or author) of every hardware component: device, firmware or device driver.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-IDENTIFIER",
              "name": "CraHardwareIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Unique identifier on every hardware component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Unique identifier on every hardware component. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every hardware component a unique identifier: a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every hardware component a unique identifier: a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-FIRMWARE-VERSION",
              "name": "CraFirmwareVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Version of every firmware component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Version of every firmware component. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every firmware component its firmware version.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every firmware component its firmware version.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-DEVICE-FIRMWARE",
              "name": "CraDeviceFirmware",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Every device has a version or a dependency on its firmware"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Every device has a version or a dependency on its firmware. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every device a version, or a dependency on the firmware component it runs.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version on the device, or add a dependencies[] entry from the device to its firmware component.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo on the device package, or add a DEPENDS_ON relationships[] entry from it to its firmware package.\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the device package, or add a dependsOn Relationship from it to its firmware package.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every device a version, or a dependency on the firmware component it runs.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version on the device, or add a dependencies\\[\\] entry from the device to its firmware component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo on the device package, or add a DEPENDS\\_ON relationships\\[\\] entry from it to its firmware package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the device package, or add a dependsOn Relationship from it to its firmware package.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-7-RQ-07-RE",
              "name": "CraVendorHashCarryThrough",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-7-RQ-07-RE]: Upstream vendor-supplied component hashes must be carried through into the SBOM"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-7-RQ-07-RE]: Upstream vendor-supplied component hashes must be carried through into the SBOM. References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].hashes[] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- SPDX 2.x: add packages[].checksums[] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- SPDX 3.0: add verifiedUsing[] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE",
                "markdown": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EUCC-PP",
              "name": "EuccProtectionProfile",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Common Criteria Protection Profile reference — sidecar eucc_protection_profile_id"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Common Criteria Protection Profile reference — sidecar eucc_protection_profile_id. References: EUCC: Protection Profile."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- EUCC: Protection Profile (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EUCC: Protection Profile](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EUCC-TOE",
              "name": "EuccTargetOfEvaluation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Target of Evaluation reference — sidecar eucc_target_of_evaluation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Target of Evaluation reference — sidecar eucc_target_of_evaluation. References: EUCC: ToE."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- EUCC: ToE (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EUCC: ToE](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EUCC-ITSEF",
              "name": "EuccItsefIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): ITSEF (IT Security Evaluation Facility) identifier — sidecar eucc_itsef_identifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): ITSEF (IT Security Evaluation Facility) identifier — sidecar eucc_itsef_identifier. References: EUCC: ITSEF."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- EUCC: ITSEF (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EUCC: ITSEF](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EUCC-VALIDITY",
              "name": "EuccCertificateValidity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): certificate valid-until date present, not expired, not near expiry — sidecar eucc_valid_until"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): certificate valid-until date present, not expired, not near expiry — sidecar eucc_valid_until. References: EUCC: Certificate validity."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- EUCC: Certificate validity (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide the Common Criteria evidence Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/482 (EUCC) expects alongside the SBOM: set euccProtectionProfileId (Protection Profile), euccTargetOfEvaluation (ToE), euccItsefIdentifier (evaluating ITSEF) and euccValidUntil (certificate validity) in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EUCC: Certificate validity](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EUCC-CERTREF",
              "name": "EuccCertificationReference",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Certification/Attestation external reference to an EUCC certificate (recommended)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EUCC (Reg. (EU) 2024/482): Certification/Attestation external reference to an EUCC certificate (recommended). References: EUCC: Certification reference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the EUCC certificate from the SBOM itself (recommended alongside the sidecar evidence).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add an externalReferences[] entry of type certification-report (or attestation) whose URL contains eucc or common-criteria, or a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field is recognized as an EUCC certificate reference.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport (or secureSoftwareAttestation) whose locator contains eucc or common-criteria.\n\nReferences:\n- EUCC: Certification reference (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the EUCC certificate from the SBOM itself (recommended alongside the sidecar evidence).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add an externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type certification-report (or attestation) whose URL contains eucc or common-criteria, or a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field is recognized as an EUCC certificate reference.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport (or secureSoftwareAttestation) whose locator contains eucc or common-criteria.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EUCC: Certification reference](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/482/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183FormatEligibility",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4: Newly generated/updated SBOMs must be CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4: Newly generated/updated SBOMs must be CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §4; BSI TR-03183-2: §7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Regenerate the SBOM as CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+ in JSON or XML. TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4 lists the eligible specifications for newly generated or updated SBOMs; the §7 transitional grace for the v2.0.0 minimums (CycloneDX 1.5 / SPDX 2.2.1) ended 2026-02-20.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §4 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §7 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Regenerate the SBOM as CycloneDX 1.6+ or SPDX 3.0.1+ in JSON or XML. TR-03183-2 v2.1.0 §4 lists the eligible specifications for newly generated or updated SBOMs; the §7 transitional grace for the v2.0.0 minimums (CycloneDX 1.5 / SPDX 2.2.1) ended 2026-02-20.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §4](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §7](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-1",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SbomCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Creator of the SBOM (email, or URL if no email)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Creator of the SBOM (email, or URL if no email). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the SBOM creator with an email address, or a URL (e.g. the creator's home page) if no email is available; generation tools do not count as the creator.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email) or metadata.manufacturer (name, contact[].email); metadata.tools entries do not count.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a creationInfo.creators[] entry such as \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\" or \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\"; Tool: entries do not count.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element that has a name; createdUsing tools do not count.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Identify the SBOM creator with an email address, or a URL (e.g. the creator's home page) if no email is available; generation tools do not count as the creator.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email) or metadata.manufacturer (name, contact\\[\\].email); metadata.tools entries do not count.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry such as \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\" or \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\"; Tool: entries do not count.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element that has a name; createdUsing tools do not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-1-CONTACT",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SbomCreatorContact",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: SBOM creator must carry an email address or URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: SBOM creator must carry an email address or URL. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add an email address to the SBOM creator entry, or a URL (creator home page / project web page) when no email exists — a bare name does not satisfy §5.2.1.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[].email, or a metadata.manufacturer contact[].email or url.\n- SPDX 2.x: append the address to the creationInfo.creators[] entry, e.g. \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\".\n- SPDX 3.0: agent emails are not read, but a creationInfo.createdBy element whose name includes an email address or URL counts.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add an email address to the SBOM creator entry, or a URL (creator home page / project web page) when no email exists — a bare name does not satisfy §5.2.1.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\].email, or a metadata.manufacturer contact\\[\\].email or url.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** append the address to the creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry, e.g. \"Person: Jane Doe (jane@example.com)\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** agent emails are not read, but a creationInfo.createdBy element whose name includes an email address or URL counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-2",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Timestamp",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Timestamp of the SBOM data compilation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.1: Timestamp of the SBOM data compilation. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add the date and time of the SBOM data compilation (UTC 'Zulu' timestamps recommended).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- SPDX 2.x: set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add the date and time of the SBOM data compilation (UTC 'Zulu' timestamps recommended).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-3",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component name (fallback: actual filename)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component name (fallback: actual filename). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name every component. When the component creator assigned no name, the actual filename MUST be used instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].name (PackageName), or files[].fileName for files.\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Name every component. When the component creator assigned no name, the actual filename MUST be used instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].name (PackageName), or files\\[\\].fileName for files.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-VERSION",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component version (fallback: RFC 3339 modification date)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component version (fallback: RFC 3339 modification date). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Version every component (SemVer/CalVer recommended). When no version is assigned, the modification date of the file as RFC 3339 date-time MUST be used instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Version every component (SemVer/CalVer recommended). When no version is assigned, the modification date of the file as RFC 3339 date-time MUST be used instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-INVENTORY",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Inventory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: SBOM lists at least one component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: SBOM lists at least one component. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component and list the components in components[].\n- SPDX 2.x: list the packages in packages[] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- SPDX 3.0: add software_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component and list the components in components\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list the packages in packages\\[\\] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add software\\_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-LICENSE",
              "name": "BsiTr03183DistributionLicence",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Distribution licence(s) per component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Distribution licence(s) per component. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2; BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the distribution licence(s) of every component, named by SPDX licence identifier or expression (§6.1).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].licenses[] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages[].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing_LicenseExpression element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Declare the distribution licence(s) of every component, named by SPDX licence identifier or expression (§6.1).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].licenses\\[\\] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages\\[\\].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing\\_LicenseExpression element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-LICENSE-SPDX",
              "name": "BsiTr03183SpdxLicenceNaming",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §6.1: Licences must be named by SPDX identifier/expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §6.1: Licences must be named by SPDX identifier/expression. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name licences by SPDX identifier or expression; consult Scancode LicenseDB (LicenseRef-scancode-*) or use LicenseRef-<entity>-* for unlisted licences. Licence text MUST NOT be used as a substitute for an identifier.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Name licences by SPDX identifier or expression; consult Scancode LicenseDB (LicenseRef-scancode-\\*) or use LicenseRef-\\<entity\\>-\\* for unlisted licences. Licence text MUST NOT be used as a substitute for an identifier.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §6.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-CREATOR",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component creator (email, or URL if no email)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Component creator (email, or URL if no email). References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record the component creator: the email address (or URL if no email) of the entity that created or maintains the component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Record the component creator: the email address (or URL if no email) of the entity that created or maintains the component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentHash",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Hash of the deployable component as SHA-512"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Hash of the deployable component as SHA-512. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide the hash of the deployed/deployable component as SHA-512 — §5.2.2 names the algorithm, so SHA-256 or other algorithms alone do not satisfy the required field (additional hashes may coexist).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a components[].hashes[] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].checksums[] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: <value>).\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Provide the hash of the deployed/deployable component as SHA-512 — §5.2.2 names the algorithm, so SHA-256 or other algorithms alone do not satisfy the required field (additional hashes may coexist).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: \\<value\\>).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-4-MISSING",
              "name": "BsiTr03183ComponentHashMissing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2/§3.2.1: Component has no hash of the deployable form"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2/§3.2.1: Component has no hash of the deployable form. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2; BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a SHA-512 hash of the deployable component. §3.2.1 permits omission only when the information cannot exist due to the way the component is assembled (e.g. logical components).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a components[].hashes[] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].checksums[] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: <value>).\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add a SHA-512 hash of the deployable component. §3.2.1 permits omission only when the information cannot exist due to the way the component is assembled (e.g. logical components).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entry with alg SHA-512.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entry with algorithm SHA512 (PackageChecksum: SHA512: \\<value\\>).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entry with algorithm sha512.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §3.2.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-5",
              "name": "BsiTr03183Dependencies",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Dependencies on other components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Dependencies on other components. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Enumerate all direct dependencies of each component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add dependencies[] entries (ref plus dependsOn[]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- SPDX 2.x: add relationships[] entries such as DEPENDS_ON (or DEPENDENCY_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- SPDX 3.0: add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Enumerate all direct dependencies of each component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add dependencies\\[\\] entries (ref plus dependsOn\\[\\]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add relationships\\[\\] entries such as DEPENDS\\_ON (or DEPENDENCY\\_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-5-COMPLETENESS",
              "name": "BsiTr03183DependencyCompleteness",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Completeness of the dependency enumeration must be clearly indicated"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.2: Completeness of the dependency enumeration must be clearly indicated. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Clearly indicate the completeness of the dependency enumeration (complete or incomplete).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set compositions[].aggregate (complete, incomplete, incomplete_first_party_only, …); the first composition is read.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field records completeness.\n- SPDX 3.0: set completeness (complete or incomplete) on the dependsOn Relationship elements.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Clearly indicate the completeness of the dependency enumeration (complete or incomplete).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set compositions\\[\\].aggregate (complete, incomplete, incomplete\\_first\\_party\\_only, …); the first composition is read.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field records completeness.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set completeness (complete or incomplete) on the dependsOn Relationship elements.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.2](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-5-2-4",
              "name": "BsiTr03183UniqueIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.4: Other unique identifiers (purl/CPE) — additional tier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §5.2.4: Other unique identifiers (purl/CPE) — additional tier. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add unique identifiers (purl, CPE) to components. §5.2.4 is the additional tier: the field MUST be provided when an identifier exists for the component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Add unique identifiers (purl, CPE) to components. §5.2.4 is the additional tier: the field MUST be provided when an identifier exists for the component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §5.2.4](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSI-TR-03183-2-3-1",
              "name": "BsiTr03183NoVulnerabilityInfo",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §3.1: An SBOM must not contain vulnerability information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI TR-03183-2 §3.1: An SBOM must not contain vulnerability information. References: BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove vulnerability information from the SBOM and publish it separately (e.g. as CSAF advisories); a document containing both SBOM and vulnerability information does not conform to TR-03183-2.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: remove the vulnerabilities[] array.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- SPDX 3.0: remove the security_Vulnerability elements and their affects and assessment Relationships.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1 (https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en)",
                "markdown": "Remove vulnerability information from the SBOM and publish it separately (e.g. as CSAF advisories); a document containing both SBOM and vulnerability information does not conform to TR-03183-2.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** remove the vulnerabilities\\[\\] array.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** remove the security\\_Vulnerability elements and their affects and assessment Relationships.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI TR-03183-2: §3.1](<https://bsi.bund.de/dok/TR-03183-en>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-1-DESCRIPTION",
              "name": "AiActModelDescription",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §1: General description of the AI model (description, architecture or model card)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §1: General description of the AI model (description, architecture or model card). References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a general description of the AI model: a description, its architecture family or name, or a model-card reference.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].description or modelCard.modelParameters.architectureFamily (or modelArchitecture), or add a model-card externalReferences[] entry.\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set description or ai_typeOfModel on the ai_AIPackage, or add a documentation externalRef[] entry.\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §1 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Add a general description of the AI model: a description, its architecture family or name, or a model-card reference.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].description or modelCard.modelParameters.architectureFamily (or modelArchitecture), or add a model-card externalReferences\\[\\] entry.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set description or ai\\_typeOfModel on the ai\\_AIPackage, or add a documentation externalRef\\[\\] entry.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §1](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-1-PURPOSE",
              "name": "AiActIntendedPurpose",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §1: Intended purpose and use-cases of the AI model"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §1: Intended purpose and use-cases of the AI model. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the intended purpose / use-cases of the AI model.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set modelCard.considerations.useCases[].\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set ai_informationAboutApplication (or ai_domain) on the ai_AIPackage.\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §1 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the intended purpose / use-cases of the AI model.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set modelCard.considerations.useCases\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set ai\\_informationAboutApplication (or ai\\_domain) on the ai\\_AIPackage.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §1](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-2D-DATASETS",
              "name": "AiActTrainingDatasets",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Training datasets referenced"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Training datasets referenced. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the training datasets used.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: list modelCard.modelParameters.datasets[] entries with a ref to each data component.\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a trainedOn Relationship from the ai_AIPackage to each dataset_DatasetPackage.\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the training datasets used.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** list modelCard.modelParameters.datasets\\[\\] entries with a ref to each data component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a trainedOn Relationship from the ai\\_AIPackage to each dataset\\_DatasetPackage.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-2D-SENSITIVITY",
              "name": "AiActDatasetSensitivity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Sensitivity classification of each dataset"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Sensitivity classification of each dataset. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare a sensitivity classification for each dataset (e.g. 'none', 'pii', 'personal').\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set data[].sensitiveData[] on each data component (the first data[] entry is read).\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set dataset_confidentialityLevel on each dataset_DatasetPackage (dataset_hasSensitivePersonalInformation yes also counts).\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare a sensitivity classification for each dataset (e.g. 'none', 'pii', 'personal').\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set data\\[\\].sensitiveData\\[\\] on each data component (the first data\\[\\] entry is read).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set dataset\\_confidentialityLevel on each dataset\\_DatasetPackage (dataset\\_hasSensitivePersonalInformation yes also counts).\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-2D-PERSONAL-DATA",
              "name": "AiActPersonalData",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Training data involving personal data (GDPR lawful basis and safeguards)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(d): Training data involving personal data (GDPR lawful basis and safeguards). References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Where training data involves personal data, document the GDPR lawful basis and data-protection measures alongside the SBOM (AI Act and GDPR apply in parallel).\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Where training data involves personal data, document the GDPR lawful basis and data-protection measures alongside the SBOM (AI Act and GDPR apply in parallel).\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(d)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-2G-METRICS",
              "name": "AiActValidationMetrics",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(g): Validation and testing metrics (accuracy, robustness)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(g): Validation and testing metrics (accuracy, robustness). References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(g)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record validation/testing metrics (accuracy, robustness).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add modelCard.quantitativeAnalysis.performanceMetrics[] entries (type, value).\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set ai_metric (or ai_metricDecisionThreshold) on the ai_AIPackage.\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(g) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Record validation/testing metrics (accuracy, robustness).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add modelCard.quantitativeAnalysis.performanceMetrics\\[\\] entries (type, value).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set ai\\_metric (or ai\\_metricDecisionThreshold) on the ai\\_AIPackage.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(g)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-2C-ENERGY",
              "name": "AiActComputationalResources",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(c): Computational resources and training-energy disclosure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §2(c): Computational resources and training-energy disclosure. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(c)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Disclose computational resources / training energy.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add modelCard.considerations.environmentalConsiderations.energyConsumptions[] entries with activity training and an activityEnergyCost.\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set ai_energyConsumption with ai_trainingEnergyConsumption entries (ai_energyQuantity, ai_energyUnit) on the ai_AIPackage.\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(c) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Disclose computational resources / training energy.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add modelCard.considerations.environmentalConsiderations.energyConsumptions\\[\\] entries with activity training and an activityEnergyCost.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set ai\\_energyConsumption with ai\\_trainingEnergyConsumption entries (ai\\_energyQuantity, ai\\_energyUnit) on the ai\\_AIPackage.\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §2(c)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-ANNEX-IV-3-LIMITATIONS",
              "name": "AiActLimitations",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §3: Foreseeable limitations and risks of the model"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act Annex IV §3: Foreseeable limitations and risks of the model. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV §3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "State the foreseeable limitations and risks of the model, including ethical and fairness considerations.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set modelCard.considerations.technicalLimitations[] (or ethicalConsiderations[], or fairnessAssessments[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: set ai_limitation on the ai_AIPackage (ai_safetyRiskAssessment, ai_modelExplainability or ai_standardCompliance also count).\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV §3 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "State the foreseeable limitations and risks of the model, including ethical and fairness considerations.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set modelCard.considerations.technicalLimitations\\[\\] (or ethicalConsiderations\\[\\], or fairnessAssessments\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set ai\\_limitation on the ai\\_AIPackage (ai\\_safetyRiskAssessment, ai\\_modelExplainability or ai\\_standardCompliance also count).\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV §3](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-AIACT-UNTYPED-ML",
              "name": "AiActUntypedMlContent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act readiness: ML content detected but not typed machine-learning-model"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EU AI Act readiness: ML content detected but not typed machine-learning-model. References: EU AI Act: Annex IV: applicability."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Components with pkg:huggingface PURLs or model-card references look like ML models; leaving them untyped hides them from every AI-BOM readiness check. Type them as machine-learning models and attach the AI metadata.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].type to machine-learning-model and add a modelCard.\n- SPDX 2.x: no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- SPDX 3.0: make the element an ai_AIPackage (or set software_primaryPurpose to model).\n\nReferences:\n- EU AI Act: Annex IV: applicability (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Components with pkg:huggingface PURLs or model-card references look like ML models; leaving them untyped hides them from every AI-BOM readiness check. Type them as machine-learning models and attach the AI metadata.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].type to machine-learning-model and add a modelCard.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no AI or dataset profile exists in this format; use CycloneDX 1.5+ or SPDX 3.0.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** make the element an ai\\_AIPackage (or set software\\_primaryPurpose to model).\n\n**References**\n\n- [EU AI Act: Annex IV: applicability](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-META-AUTHOR",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiAuthor",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM author"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM author. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Author."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- SPDX 2.x: add creationInfo.creators[] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Author (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Author](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-META-FORMAT",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiDataFormat",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: Data-format name and version"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: Data-format name and version. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Data format name + version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Data format name + version (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Data format name + version](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-META-TIMESTAMP",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiTimestamp",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM timestamp"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM timestamp. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Timestamp."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- SPDX 2.x: set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Timestamp (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.timestamp (RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-01-15T10:00:00Z).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set creationInfo.created (Created).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.created on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Timestamp](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-META-TOOL",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiGenerationTool",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: Generation tool"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: Generation tool. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Generation tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.tools with the tool's name and version.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a creationInfo.creators[] entry \"Tool: <name>-<version>\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdUsing to a Tool element whose name includes the version.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Generation tool (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.tools with the tool's name and version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry \"Tool: \\<name\\>-\\<version\\>\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdUsing to a Tool element whose name includes the version.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Generation tool](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-META-SIGNATURE",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiSignature",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM signature"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI Metadata: SBOM signature. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Signature."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: sign the BOM: in JSON, a JSF signature object (algorithm and value) at the document root; in XML, an enveloped XML-DSig <Signature> element on <bom>.\n- SPDX 2.x: no in-document signature field exists.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] entry of type signature (algorithm, hashValue) to the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Signature (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** sign the BOM: in JSON, a JSF signature object (algorithm and value) at the document root; in XML, an enveloped XML-DSig \\<Signature\\> element on \\<bom\\>.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no in-document signature field exists.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] entry of type signature (algorithm, hashValue) to the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: Metadata / Signature](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-SYS-PRIMARY",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiPrimarySystem",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI System-Level: Primary AI system identified"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI System-Level: Primary AI system identified. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Primary AI system."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- SPDX 2.x: name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- SPDX 3.0: set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Primary AI system (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Primary AI system](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-SYS-PRODUCER",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiProducer",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI System-Level: Producer of the AI system"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI System-Level: Producer of the AI system. References: BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Producer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Producer (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements)",
                "markdown": "Declare the BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI minimum elements: document author, data-format name + version, timestamp, generation tool, and signature; the primary AI system, its producer, and its data-flow/usage; runtime/framework infrastructure links; and AI-specific security controls / exploitability references where they can be expressed.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [BSI/G7 AI-SBOM: System-Level / Producer](<https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/software-bill-materials-ai-minimum-elements>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-BSIAI-SYS-DATAFLOW",
              "name": "BsiSbomForAiDataFlow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BSI/G7 SBOM-for-AI System-Level: Data flow and usage of the AI system"
              },
